WEBVTT

1
00:00:09.946 --> 00:00:16.992
Long ago, before the gods ruled on Mount Olympus, before humans walked the earth, the Titans brought the

2
00:00:17.032 --> 00:00:18.213
world out of chaos.

3
00:00:19.294 --> 00:00:23.557
They were the children of Uranus, the sky, and Gaia, the earth.

4
00:00:24.598 --> 00:00:31.124
They ruled the world with benevolence, and lived among its oceans, fields, and mountains during a golden age.

5
00:00:32.224 --> 00:00:38.989
Cronus, the youngest, battled his father to become ruler of the Titans, and then, with his sister Rhea

6
00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:41.671
as his wife, he fathered many children.

7
00:00:42.471 --> 00:00:48.696
His mother had warned him, however, that his own son would one day overthrow him, just as he

8
00:00:48.736 --> 00:00:50.036
had defeated Uranus.

9
00:00:51.397 --> 00:00:57.261
So, as each of his children was born, he picked the baby up and swallowed the infant whole.

10
00:00:58.302 --> 00:01:04.246
Only his youngest son, Zeus, was saved, when Rhea tricked her husband by giving him a stone wrapped

11
00:01:04.306 --> 00:01:06.228
in a blanket to swallow instead.

12
00:01:07.649 --> 00:01:12.992
Rhea sent Zeus away to the island of Crete, where he could grow up safely in secret.

13
00:01:13.793 --> 00:01:18.176
He was raised on goats' milk and honey and learned to be a fierce warrior.

14
00:01:19.016 --> 00:01:23.099
When Zeus was old enough, he returned to seek vengeance on his father.

15
00:01:24.020 --> 00:01:29.864
After a long and mighty struggle, he defeated Cronus and the many Titans who fought alongside him.

16
00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:37.483
Then he plunged his sword into his father's abdomen, sliced his belly open, and released his brothers and

17
00:01:37.543 --> 00:01:42.825
sisters. Zeus became the king of the gods and ruled the Olympians.

18
00:01:43.666 --> 00:01:50.449
He condemned the defeated Titans to the underworld, but permitted those few who had not fought alongside Cronus

19
00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:52.650
to live at the foot of the mountain.

20
00:01:53.450 --> 00:02:00.501
Of these, the brothers Prometheus and Epimetheus were Zeus' favorites, and he allowed them many freedoms.

21
00:02:01.362 --> 00:02:07.545
Epimetheus was grateful and satisfied with his new life, but the clever Prometheus grew bored.

22
00:02:08.325 --> 00:02:14.809
The inventive Titan needed something to entertain him, so one day, he picked up a handful of clay

23
00:02:15.289 --> 00:02:17.370
and molded it into the shape of a man.

24
00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:23.974
Prometheus made many men, giving them each two legs, two arms, and five senses.

25
00:02:24.975 --> 00:02:29.521
Then Athena, the goddess of wisdom, breathed life into these shapes.

26
00:02:30.581 --> 00:02:35.383
Soon, the men learned to cook food, build homes, and survive on their own.

27
00:02:36.504 --> 00:02:43.547
Zeus watched with a wary eye as these new beings flourished, but Prometheus was aware of his unease.

28
00:02:44.527 --> 00:02:49.789
To keep his creations safe from Zeus' wrath, he taught the men to worship the king of the

29
00:02:49.829 --> 00:02:56.152
gods, and he showed them how to build temples and sacrifice animals to the deities of Mount Olympus.

30
00:02:56.992 --> 00:03:02.957
For a long time, the men appeased Zeus with their reverence, but the quiet did not last.

31
00:03:04.118 --> 00:03:08.081
One night, the leader of the men came to Prometheus with a request.

32
00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:14.767
Men were hungry for the taste of meat, and Prometheus' visitor begged him to let them eat the

33
00:03:14.827 --> 00:03:16.048
sacrificial animals.

34
00:03:16.948 --> 00:03:22.032
Prometheus, who loved these beings very much, did not want to see them unhappy.

35
00:03:22.853 --> 00:03:26.216
So he told them to give him the animal for their next sacrifice.

36
00:03:27.124 --> 00:03:33.227
He took the meat and divided it into two piles: the first pile contained all the good meat,

37
00:03:33.727 --> 00:03:40.930
but covered by the animal's unappetizing stomach and innards; the second pile was only bones, hidden under a

38
00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.971
delectable layer of juicy fat.

39
00:03:44.111 --> 00:03:49.654
When Zeus came to judge which portion should be for the gods and which for the men, he

40
00:03:49.714 --> 00:03:51.554
chose, of course, the second pile.

41
00:03:52.515 --> 00:03:58.325
When he returned with it to Mount Olympus and discovered that he had been fooled, he burst into

42
00:03:58.385 --> 00:03:58.885
a rage.

43
00:03:59.985 --> 00:04:05.427
From his mountain peak, he sent thunderbolts and a fierce rain down onto the earth below.

44
00:04:06.447 --> 00:04:12.349
Prometheus visited the men after the storm and was distraught to see them huddled together in misery.

45
00:04:13.449 --> 00:04:15.209
The men were cold and hungry.

46
00:04:16.050 --> 00:04:23.552
Prometheus asked Epimetheus to watch over his suffering creations and then, quickly and quietly, climbed to the top

47
00:04:23.592 --> 00:04:24.472
of Mount Olympus.

48
00:04:25.508 --> 00:04:31.411
At the summit, he snatched a bundle of burning branches from Zeus' hearth and hurried back down the

49
00:04:31.431 --> 00:04:34.953
mountain. He passed the god's fire to the men.

50
00:04:36.134 --> 00:04:41.437
When Prometheus returned to his home at the base of Mount Olympus, he found the king of the

51
00:04:41.497 --> 00:04:42.737
gods blocking the way.

52
00:04:43.818 --> 00:04:48.360
Zeus grabbed Prometheus by the neck and lifted him high off the ground.

53
00:04:49.181 --> 00:04:55.497
Then he hurled the Titan into the underworld, calling on Hades, the god of the underworld, to punish

54
00:04:55.557 --> 00:04:57.678
Prometheus with an eternity of pain.

55
00:04:58.459 --> 00:05:04.464
Prometheus was chained to a tall rock, and every morning, a great eagle tore his liver from his

56
00:05:04.524 --> 00:05:09.688
body, only for it to grow back each night and be plucked out again the next day.

57
00:05:10.569 --> 00:05:17.294
Epimetheus was devastated by his brother's punishment, but thankful to have escaped Zeus' retribution himself.

58
00:05:18.175 --> 00:05:22.839
Zeus, however, was plotting a very different sort of punishment for Epimetheus.

59
00:05:23.839 --> 00:05:30.423
First, Zeus paid a visit to the god of fire and forge, Hephaestus, and demanded that he create

60
00:05:30.443 --> 00:05:31.384
a mortal woman.

61
00:05:32.444 --> 00:05:36.547
Then, he asked his fellow gods and goddesses to adorn her with gifts.

62
00:05:37.807 --> 00:05:44.651
Aphrodite, the goddess of love, gave her the beauty to attract any man to her side; Athena gave

63
00:05:44.691 --> 00:05:50.474
her the skills she would need on earth; and Hermes, the messenger of the gods, gave her the

64
00:05:50.534 --> 00:05:51.495
power of speech.

65
00:05:52.375 --> 00:05:53.796
They named her Pandora.

66
00:05:54.292 --> 00:05:57.494
Her final gift came from Zeus: a sealed jar.

67
00:05:58.234 --> 00:06:04.678
Prometheus had long warned his brother not to accept gifts from the gods, but when Zeus presented Pandora

68
00:06:04.718 --> 00:06:09.080
to him, Epimetheus was captivated by her beauty and eloquence.

69
00:06:10.141 --> 00:06:16.304
They were married within days, and the humans rejoiced at the favor Zeus had shown to their protector.

70
00:06:17.224 --> 00:06:24.620
Epimetheus asked Pandora about the jar, and she explained that Zeus had given her explicit instructions that the

71
00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:27.443
jar was to be admired but never opened.

72
00:06:28.444 --> 00:06:33.548
Epimetheus took the jar and placed it high on a shelf in his home, where he could look

73
00:06:33.628 --> 00:06:34.508
upon it fondly.

74
00:06:35.529 --> 00:06:39.072
Pandora was beautiful and intelligent and loved to learn.

75
00:06:39.733 --> 00:06:44.276
She explored nearby mountains and discovered new herbs to grow in the garden.

76
00:06:45.077 --> 00:06:50.942
She read the tablets carved in the temples and understood the importance of sacrificing to the gods.

77
00:06:51.883 --> 00:06:53.164
She was always curious.

78
00:06:53.948 --> 00:06:58.952
So when she looked at the jar sitting on the shelf, she wondered what secrets it held.

79
00:07:00.013 --> 00:07:01.174
"What could be inside?"

80
00:07:01.715 --> 00:07:02.575
she asked herself.

81
00:07:02.596 --> 00:07:05.678
"Why did Zeus tell us never to open it?"

82
00:07:06.519 --> 00:07:10.722
Pandora reached up and lifted the jar from its perch on the shelf.

83
00:07:11.603 --> 00:07:17.108
Holding it carefully in her hands, she carried it to a chair by the fireplace and sat down.

84
00:07:17.948 --> 00:07:24.418
Pandora knew she should not defy the wishes of Zeus and her husband, but her curiosity overwhelmed her.

85
00:07:25.559 --> 00:07:30.543
Slowly, she loosened the lid and lifted it just enough to peek inside.

86
00:07:31.443 --> 00:07:33.585
A great force rushed from the jar!

87
00:07:34.406 --> 00:07:41.191
In a thick, black cloud, all the evils of the world poured out: hatred, jealousy, fear, greed, and

88
00:07:41.291 --> 00:07:48.957
anger. Pandora quickly realized her mistake and slammed the lid back on the jar, trapping one last item

89
00:07:48.977 --> 00:07:53.113
inside. Watching from Mount Olympus, Zeus smiled.

90
00:07:53.793 --> 00:08:00.937
His punishment was complete; humankind would be beset with strife and plagued by sorrow for all eternity.

91
00:08:01.657 --> 00:08:06.199
Pandora carefully replaced the jar on the shelf with its one treasure still inside.

92
00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:09.261
Inside the jar remained hope.
